    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d274">

                <pb facs="0383" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg263"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                        Squiers.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 460.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose copy of a letter from A. W.
                    Pinkham, of Lynn, Mass., to the Hon. E. W. Roberts, a member of the House of
                        Representatives,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d274-f1"/> regarding the proposed
                    enforcement of a law in Cuba requiring a statement of the formula of patent
                    medicines in order to obtain authorization for their sale.</p>
                <p>The complainant represents that if the law is enfofced, he will nave to withdraw
                    from the sale of his preparations in Cuba.</p>
                <p>You may use your good offices in the matter and report to the Department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis B.
                    Loomis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
